    "peak": "Tool publication peaked in the 2000-2004 period with 89 tools, coinciding with the genomics revolution and the rise of Bayesian phylogenetics.",
    "languages": "C dominates the catalog (90 tools), followed by Java (60), reflecting the computational demands of phylogenetic inference and the era in which most tools were written."
